/*
  TeslaApiUsageCard.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0257 · TeslaApiUsageCard (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native `TeslaApiUsageCard`
  resolves (table "TeslaApiUsageCard") lives here with its web English value. These entries fold
  into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept in a
  per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without editing the shared
  catalog.

  The web source (features/system/components/status/TeslaApiUsageCard.tsx feeding
  components/data-display/UsageCard.tsx) uses hardcoded English literals (no t() calls — the surface
  is "anonymous"). Per the native no-English-literals rule, every one of those literals is promoted
  to a key here. The first group is the parity set extracted from the web source; the second group
  backs the native chrome (the P4 leaf freshness / loading / error copy + the card title) so the
  Swift sources hold no English prose literals.
*/

